<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan dollar ends unchanged.</title>
<headline>Taiwan dollar ends unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan dollar closed unchanged against the U.S. dollar on Monday as year-end commercial demand for the American currency was offset by abundant supply, dealers said.</p>
<p>The local dollar finished at T$27.500, unchanged from Saturday's close. Turnover through dealers was US$174.5 million.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite year-end demand for the U.S. dollar continuing to emerge, many exporters are willing to sell (the) greenback at the current level,&quot; said one dealer. &quot;It will surprise me if the rate moves sharply before the end of the year.&quot;</p>
<p>A narrow T$27.490-505 range was seen for Tuesday.</p>
<p>-Alice Hung(5080815)</p>
